  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In quadrilateral \\(ABCD,\\) \\(AB = 5,\\) \\(BC = 17,\\) \\(CD = 5,\\) \\(DA = 9,\\) and \\(BD\\) is an integer. What is \\(BD?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(11\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(13\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(14\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(15\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "13"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2009-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "In \\(\\triangle BCD,\\) the triangle inequality gives \\(BD + CD \\gt BC,\\) so \\(BD + 5 \\gt 17\\) and \\(BD \\gt 12.\\)\n\nIn \\(\\triangle ABD,\\) \\(AB + DA \\gt BD,\\) so \\(BD \\lt 5 + 9 = 14.\\)\n\nThe only integer with \\(12 \\lt BD \\lt 14\\) is \\(13.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Apply the triangle inequality to \\(\\triangle BCD\\) and \\(\\triangle ABD\\)",
        "From \\(\\triangle BCD,\\) \\(BD \\gt 12,\\) and from \\(\\triangle ABD,\\) \\(BD \\lt 14\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
